  "id": "chunk_24",
  "chunk": "ended. Recall that the game ends when (i) the maximum score is achieved, (ii)\nthe player dies, or (iii) the LLM provides the command ‘I give up’. Interestingly,\nalthough ChatGPT performed the worst in terms of overall game progress, it\nrefuses to give up, as indicated by the average number of moves until (ii) or (iii)\nare reached. Indeed, further inspection reveals that ChatGPT often finds itself\nin long series of similar commands resulting in no measurable progress (i.e., the\n7\nplayer was stuck), hinting at no useful form of metacognition. To a lesser extent\nthis also holds for the other LLMs, where —due to further advancing in the\ngame— they found themselves more likely to be killed, either due to bad luck\nor due to improper game play (e.g., not killing a monster while its unarmed and\nstunned on the ground). Further analysis shows that only Claude issued the\ncommand ‘I give up’ when it appeared to find itself in a vicious circle it could\nnot escape.\n5 Discussion",
